  {
    "episode_id": 86579,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86579.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 54,
    "turn_text": "I think that this is an issue where, again, you've got broad public support that if you have an infant who can feel pain, it's capable, and in some instances, you sort of see the resisting, resisting the incursion, the instrument that's used to commit the abortion, the infant is trying to, they know that this is dangerous to them, they're able to feel pain. I think that most people can agree then, you know what? Abortion should not take place in those circumstances, except to save the life of the mother. But that, I think, is an area where there's broad public agreement. We ought to be able to agree on that. And those of us, and move forward, and those of us in the pro-life movement ought to say, okay, let's find those areas of consensus. Let's get those, and then continue the process of persuasion.",
