    "turn_text": "her and of her service. But I will say this, I think that when it comes to open hostilities, declaration of war, the first and most important consideration is we have to protect American lives. I mean, so first and foremost, our military is there to protect this country, to protect American citizens. And so that's the first question, I think. And then beyond that, our vital interests, and then our allies, like for instance, the state of Israel. One of the things that I think is shameful from the last 10 years, the previous president's term, and I'm sorry to say Senator McCaskill supported him to the health of this, was to sell out Israel with the Iran treaty, which I think is a disastrous piece of foreign policy. It weakened this country. It weakened our allies. It weakened our standing in the world and our commitment to freedom. So I think that we've got to stand strong with our allies, but above all, we've got to look to protecting America's interests and American citizens and American lives.",
